  "body": "The groups/communities feature in Synapse is unspecced (defined in [MSC1513](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/issues/1513), kind of, but is abandoned) -- spaces ([MSC1772](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/pull/1772) and friends).\r\n\r\nThere are still some useful features driven by Groups (namely flair) so it is unclear when this will happen. Note that Element Web has the capability to convert a Group -> Space.\r\n\r\nA rough plan of how we might want to do this is:\r\n\r\n* [x] Add an experimental config flag for groups that guards the unstable endpoints for groups.\r\n* [x] Add a deprecation notice to our release and upgrade notes. (Should probably be done at the same time as 1.)\r\n* [x] Default the above flag to `false` to disable those endpoints at the end of the deprecation period. The configuration flag should emit a warning if it is enabled.\r\n* [x] (After some time...) Remove the groups code.\r\n\t* Endpoints\r\n\t* Handlers\r\n\t* Update the worker documentation\r\n\t* `RelatedGroups` constant\r\n* [x] (After some time...) Bump the schema and remove the database tables for groups.\r\n\r\nRelated to #8334.",
